WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:02.980
You're closing shop, huh?

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:04.280
Yeah...

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.860
We wanted to do our best to stay 
open while we still had regulars,

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.400
but we're getting old, 
and sales aren't great.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:13.900
Most drink tea from plastic 
bottles these days.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.280
Not many people bother with teapots anymore.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.080
Right.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:23.710
My wife and I have been thinking maybe 
it's a good time to call it quits.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.660
We don't have anyone to take over the shop.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.920
Rokuhoudou has been good to us 
since Kyounosuke-san's time.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.640
We've had a spectacular run.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.900
Thank you so much.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.750
Likewise.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:55.030
Thank you for all the delicious tea.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:01.420
So, with that, I'd like to introduce 
you to a long-time acquaintance

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:04.450
that you can work with in our place,

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:07.750
though they're a little difficult.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:09.500
Difficult?

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.000
Don't tell me it's the infamous...

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.360
"Infamous"?

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.430
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.560
<b>"The Teahouse's Secrets"</b>

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.060
Dude, Sui, what do you mean by "infamous"?

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.520
Oh, you mean what I said earlier.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:56.080
Oh yeah, we got busy right after.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.940
We didn't get a chance to ask Itou-san.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:02.610
I was so curious, my mind was wandering 
the whole time during work.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.620
Like, maybe they threaten customers 
to make them buy pricey tea.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.620
Or maybe they trade firearms under 
the cover of being a teahouse.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.920
Me, too, actually.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:16.430
They've been powerful in the 
tea business for generations,

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:20.190
and the sudden death of their boss 
triggers a messy succession battle.

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:21.970
One by one, the members of the family vanish,

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.230
just as foretold in a creepy tea-serving 
song that had been passed down over the ages.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:26.320
And when no one is left,

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.910
the shocking truth that had been buried 
in the basement of the shop is revealed!

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.770
You guys both watch way too 
many movies and dramas.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.190
So, what's the real reason it's infamous?

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:39.600
It's actually nothing that huge.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:40.940
But...

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.230
But?

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:45.200
A kettle flew in someone's direction 
the moment they set foot in the shop.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.810
There's always some shattered 
debris on the floor.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.330
Someone's apparently been tied 
down with a rope or something.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:55.480
There are tons of such rumors, 
but I hear nothing about the tea.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:58.020
And what is the shop called?

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.550
Well, you see...

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.050
I don't remember.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:06.430
<i>You don't?!</i>

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.430
That was delicious.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.550
Let's come for dinner next time.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:14.170
T-Today's the day.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:22.270
We need to start choosing a new tea shop.

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:26.190
Yes, but I just can't find a good tea shop.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:27.740
Hey, if worse comes to worst,

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.640
I'll keep us alive with my coffee.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:39.380
Hey, what was that, Tsubaki-kun?

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.260
Um...

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.730
Would you like to come inside?

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:08.270
<i>Which is it?</i>

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.170
She's been like that for at least 
twenty minutes now, hasn't she?

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:25.630
It's actually been thirty minutes.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.390
U-Um...

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:33.690
Here you are.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:37.140
Matcha warabi-mochi and mini-anmitsu set.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.560
Enjoy.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:43.110
Time to eat.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:03.090
She makes a good face.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:06.150
Tsubaki-kun's warabi-mochi 
must have really hit the spot.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:13.350
What are you so happy about, Tsubaki-kun?

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:14.700
Nothing.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.110
Out of a thousand yen.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.190
Was it not to your liking?

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:11.280
No, that's not it at all.

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:14.180
I-It was really delicious.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:17.540
It really was delicious!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.870
Um, the tea here...

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:25.430
It's old man Itou's, isn't it?

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:27.500
Yes.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.580
I'm impressed that you could tell.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:32.970
They make a special blend for us.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:37.260
I can taste the combination 
of the Gyokusui and Meisui.

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:41.470
Miss, you can tell just from the taste?

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:44.730
Thank you.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.670
N-Nice to meet you.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:52.740
Are you all right?

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:57.330
No, no, no thank you very much.

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:58.850
What's going on?

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.580
Thank you.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:05.580
Gure.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:06.840
Me?

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:11.970
That girl guessed the tea leaves 
we use just by the taste.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:14.250
That's impressive.

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.050
Do you think she'll be back again?

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.690
That was probably Gure's fault.

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:22.020
Tsubaki-kun's blaming me again.

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:23.860
Take this!

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:24.680
Nah.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:25.320
Stop it!

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:31.020
I think she might be back 
sooner than you think.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.240
<b>Closed</b>

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.620
Do you <i>have</i> to go to that tea shop?

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:46.460
Yes.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:48.640
I thought I'd at least say hi.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.630
I'll be back by evening.

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:53.630
See you.

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:55.330
Take care.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:02.540
<i>That shop is infamous...</i>

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.520
<i>Is Sui going to be all 
right going by himself?</i>

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:08.770
<i>What if any of those things happened?</i>

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:14.410
Uh, Tokitaka-kun?

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.910
Is this what you left behind?

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:25.630
Yes, thank you.

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:27.880
I thought you'd be back to get it.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:30.100
Thank you.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:32.830
U-Um, I...

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:35.590
That was rude of me the other day,

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:38.300
blurting out what kind of tea it was.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.740
Not at all.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:41.730
You were right.

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:45.200
Our tea leaves are a blend 
of Gyokusui and Meisui.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:46.560
How could you tell?

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:50.060
My grandparents' family 
knows a lot about tea.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:52.440
I've been drinking a lot since I was little.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:57.830
My family would have tea-tasting 
parties once a week,

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:01.510
and I would try blending tea 
to my own liking and stuff.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:05.230
My grandpa took me on a 
tea farm tour across Japan

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:07.010
to learn about tea making.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:10.230
Your family sounds quite 
passionate about tea.

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:14.380
Then the reason you looked so bothered 
as you were having tea the other day...

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:17.480
Did I really?

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:18.880
<i>She didn't notice?</i>

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:23.060
No, the tea was very delicious.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:24.890
But if...

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:28.890
If that tea was my...

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:32.920
S-Sorry to take time out of your day off.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:33.910
I'll be leaving.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:35.490
Sorry for staying so long.

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.100
I'll take you home.

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:44.100
It's dangerous to walk alone in the evening.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.000
Thank you.

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:48.180
No problem.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:50.250
I was about to go out, too.

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:55.670
Hey, about what I said earlier...

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:56.330
Yes?

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:59.780
That time, I was... How do I put it?

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:06.530
If that tea was from my grandpa's shop,

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:09.140
I would have been so happy.

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:11.150
So then you're...

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:14.150
My grandfather runs a tea shop.

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:18.150
But they're losing customers fast.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:21.160
So I wanted to know if there 
was anything I could do.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:25.240
I've been looking for a tea shop, 
and I found Rokuhoudou.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:28.540
S-Sorry, that was a weird thing to say.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:31.190
I can go from here.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:32.870
My home is nearby.

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:35.250
By the McValue just over there.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.130
<b>Amagamiya</b>

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:44.080
To think you were the granddaughter of the 
tea shop owner that I was about to visit...

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:44.760
Yes.

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:48.310
<i>It doesn't seem as scary 
as the rumors suggest.</i>

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:52.650
Grandpa, we have a guest.

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:56.230
Wh-What was that?

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:58.900
Don't stop me, Sae!

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:01.150
I'm quitting!

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.030
G-Grandpa...

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:06.350
What is it, Kotsuru?

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.330
Who's that man?

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:19.090
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:17.150
Rokuhoudou.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.670
Sorry, but I'll have you leave.

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:23.760
But...

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:27.710
Kotsuru, Amagamiya is closing as of today.

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:31.270
Oh, welcome home.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.950
Grandma, what's going on?

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:35.770
I never heard you were closing.

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:38.700
One of our café clients said

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:41.860
they can get their tea in teabags,
which are cheaper,

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:45.530
so they don't need us anymore.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:48.210
Oh, I'm sorry about the fuss.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:51.790
Tea packs my ass... What an insult!

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.190
They don't need our tea?

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:56.210
We're too behind the times? Unprofitable?

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:58.050
Don't give me that BS!

00:12:58.050 --> 00:12:59.800
Grandpa, calm down!

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:00.720
<i>I see.</i>

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:03.770
<i>So this intense old man is 
the source of the rumors.</i>

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:07.250
How dare they call themselves a café 
when they don't even serve good tea?

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:05.700
Come on, Grandpa.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:06.680
Um...

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.300
No, I er...

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:09.300
How dare you call it "work" 
when you're cutting corners?

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.210
Grandpa!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.700
Don't you have any honor?

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:12.470
Calm down, Grandpa!

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.680
I'm calm!

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:20.500
They're proving they don't 
even know anything about tea!

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:24.730
Damn it! Isn't there anyone 
who has a proper palate?!

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:26.200
Um...

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:30.800
To hell with this!

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:31.930
I'm quitting!

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:33.790
Amagamiya is closing as of today!

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:36.450
Grandpa...

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:40.250
I love this shop.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:44.020
I'm sure we'll find someone who 
understands, if we search hard enough.

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:45.260
Kotsuru...

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:49.500
Not everyone drinks tea like you do anymore.

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:50.390
But...

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:55.390
I'd rather have no one drink tea 
than let them drink half-mindedly.

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.110
Stuck in the past?

00:13:57.110 --> 00:14:00.810
If you don't need me, you might 
as well just vanish with me.

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:03.530
No one needs us anymore.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.990
If you don't need it, sir...

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.070
<b>Okuharuno
 Touge no Kaori</b>

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:12.130
May I have it?

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:13.080
What?

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:14.940
No, no.

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:18.200
I'm not letting some brat who doesn't 
even understand tea have my tea.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:21.390
Even if I've decided I'm 
not selling it anymore.

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:22.950
Sorry, but go away.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:24.600
Grandpa, that's rude.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:25.890
This man's shop is...

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:28.130
Well, that's a pickle.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:33.460
I saw your tea and wanted very 
much to use it at our shop.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:37.760
My tea isn't that cheap.

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:39.400
I can see that.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.880
It seems I'm going to have 
to win your approval first.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.400
But I still haven't decided

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:51.410
whether or not your tea would 
truly be appropriate for my shop.

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:57.430
Do you really think my tea wouldn't 
be good enough for you, Glasses?

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:04.760
How about we play a game?

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:14.010
We'd like to use your tea leaves 
at our shop for just one day.

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:17.520
I'll invite you over that day.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.240
Let's decide together if we're 
appropriate for each other.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:23.020
If you approve of my café, I win.

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:26.350
I'll then have the right to decide 
whether or not we use your tea.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:29.540
If I approve of your tea, you win.

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:32.070
What you would like to 
do, then, is up to you.

00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:34.510
Damn brat.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:36.640
You want to test my tea?

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:38.080
How insulting.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.300
Do you have any idea how 
long I've been making tea?

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:42.080
What "game"? Cocky brat.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.770
Having trouble sleeping?

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:53.420
Yes. A little.

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:56.730
It was good tea.

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:02.100
You aren't the only one 
having trouble sleeping.

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:06.850
Amagamiya's tea seems to have inspired

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:11.230
Tsubaki-kun and Gure-kun to 
stay up all night tonight.

00:16:14.270 --> 00:16:16.310
Let's hope we can protect it...

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:20.580
The act of serving someone tea with heart.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.670
Even if it's an outdated idea,

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:26.670
it seems to me to be indispensable.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:37.200
Kyousui...

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:39.430
Do you like this shop?

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:40.720
Yeah.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:42.250
You do, huh?

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.170
Well, then...

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:46.340
Yes.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.360
We need to protect it.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.460
So where's the man's shop?

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:57.410
Um...

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:58.420
There.

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:11.280
This place...

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:17.220
See?

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:18.680
It's nice here, isn't it?

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:21.720
Amagami-san, Kotsuru-san.

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:25.350
Thank you for coming today.

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:28.160
I'm here to see what you're made of.

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:29.840
Let's begin.

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:43.950
Amagamiya's green tea and chiffon cake.

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:47.420
Our patissier came up with 
it to match the tea.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:49.040
Please, if you'd like.

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:50.860
Thank you.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:59.810
I just want the tea.

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:01.270
No, Grandpa!

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:02.710
You have to try this!

00:18:02.710 --> 00:18:03.910
No, I'm good.

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:04.610
Just try it!

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:05.850
I—

00:18:07.930 --> 00:18:09.860
Are these our tea leaves?

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:10.810
Yeah.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.960
They mixed it in in fine grains.

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:15.140
You can really taste the tea.

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:17.600
The mild bitterness is nice, too.

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:07.640
Hey, Glasses...

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:08.160
Yes?

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:10.960
Are you Kyounosuke-san's grandson?

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:14.710
You know of my grandfather?

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:16.120
Yeah.

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:18.900
I've been here just once, way back.

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:22.830
I couldn't decide if I should 
take over the shop, when...

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:42.980
That man's tea gave me a 
gentle push in the back.

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:50.850
Your tea has a warmth kind of like his.

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:57.530
And you, patissier...

00:19:57.530 --> 00:19:58.670
Y-Yes?

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:01.970
How dare you mince my precious tea?

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.530
Well...

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:05.850
Because the leaves have a very nice scent,

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:09.980
I thought it might work better with 
the chiffon than matcha, so...

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:12.780
You ought to use less tea in it.

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:16.540
That'll make it easier for kids.

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:19.610
Besides that, you do good work.

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:25.900
I hate to admit it, but it's a nice shop.

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:27.200
You win.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.200
No, you win.

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:33.780
Calling it a "game" was snotty of me.

00:20:33.780 --> 00:20:38.430
But the game was over the moment 
I set foot in your store.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:43.510
The tea was excellent, of course, 
but the atmosphere in the store,

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:46.890
the commitment, and more than anything,

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.560
having seen Kotsuru-san,

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:55.200
it was plain to see how much 
love you've put into your tea.

00:20:55.930 --> 00:20:59.790
I accept my loss, and would 
like to plead with you

00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:02.320
to let us use your tea.

00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:21.650
I feel like I've had my back pushed again.

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:55.390
<b>Amagamiya</b>

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:55.390
Sorry, but go away.

00:22:55.390 --> 00:22:58.190
I think it's a good deal.

00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:01.440
My shop is good enough.

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:05.010
We just earned another regular recently.

00:23:05.010 --> 00:23:05.860
Oh?

00:23:05.860 --> 00:23:06.690
Where's that?

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:09.700
Rokuhoudou, one town over.

00:23:10.650 --> 00:23:13.570
Oh? Rokuhoudou?

00:23:15.570 --> 00:23:16.800
Look, look, Tsubaki-kun!

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:30.170
<b>Next episode</b>

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:30.170
<b>"Sweets Trap Collection"</b>

00:23:16.800 --> 00:23:18.720
I managed to get my hands 
on a tea tree sapling.

00:23:18.720 --> 00:23:19.760
What are you even going to do with it?

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:20.840
Grow it.

00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:22.440
First, we're buying 20,000 hectares of land.

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:24.750
That's more than all the tea 
farms in Shizuoka combined.

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:27.340
Want to make Rokuhoudou 
Japan's biggest tea producer?

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:30.170
<b>Come again soon.</b>

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:28.730
We won't make it!
